.TH tutablepng n 0.1 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tutablepng
.PP
Render tabular data to a PNG table image using the pure\-Tcl drawing layer \fBtclutils::tupngdraw\fR (no Tk, no external packages). An export adapter: data in, a styled table image out.
.SS API
.CS
package require tclutils::tutablepng

::tclutils::tutablepng::render rows ?options?   ;# -> PNG bytes
::tclutils::tutablepng::write  file rows ?options?  ;# -> file
.CE
.PP
\fBrows\fR is a list of rows; each row is a list of cell strings. Short rows are padded with empty cells; the column count is the widest row.
.PP
Options (defaults): \fB\-header 1\fR (style the first row), \fB\-align l\fR (a single \fBl|c|r\fR or a per\-column list), \fB\-scale 1\fR (font scale), \fB\-padding 6\fR (cell padding px), \fB\-spacing 1\fR (px between glyphs), \fB\-background white\fR, \fB\-gridcolor {180 180 185}\fR, \fB\-textcolor {25 25 25}\fR, \fB\-headerbg {230 230 238}\fR, \fB\-headertext {0 0 0}\fR, \fB\-zebra {}\fR (alt\-row colour, empty = off), \fB\-border 1\fR (grid lines). Colours take any tupngdraw form (name, \fB#rrggbb\fR, \fBRRGGBB\fR, \fB{r g b}\fR, \fB{r g b a}\fR).
.CS
set rows {
    {Name      Qty Price}
    {Apples     12  3.40}
    {Pears        4  2.10}
}
tclutils::tutablepng::write table.png $rows \
    -header 1 -align {l r r} -zebra {245 245 248}
.CE
.SS CLI
.CS
tclsh bin/tutablepng.tcl out.png -d , -header 1 -align "l r r" data.csv
cat data.tsv | tclsh bin/tutablepng.tcl out.png
.CE
.PP
Reads delimited rows (default delimiter: tab) from a file or stdin and writes a PNG table.
.SS Notes
.PP
Column widths are derived from the fixed 6x8 font, so they are exact for the embedded glyphs. Grid lines are drawn crisp (no antialiasing); cell text is the bitmap font. For large tables prefer a modest \fB\-scale\fR.
